From 3ffeb443f89f7175cb0e0b34baebcec61f1925bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wray-lee <wray-lee@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:39:40 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(providers): send /think levels to OpenAI-compatible
 models and add max

/think and the config reasoning_effort only reached OpenAI reasoning models:
appendGenerationFields drops the field for every model isReasoningModel does
not recognise, so on DeepSeek, Kimi, K2 and other OpenAI-compatible models
behind the compatible provider the level was silently ignored. Those endpoints
take the same top-level reasoning_effort field.

- The compatible provider now sends the chosen level to such models
  (minimal -> low; xhigh and max pass through). Providers that map
  reasoning_effort to their own field (GLM thinking, Qwen enable_thinking,
  MiniMax reasoning_split, vLLM chat_template_kwargs) are unchanged.
- When the endpoint rejects the field ("Invalid value for 'reasoning_effort'"),
  the provider learns a limit for that model and resends: a level above high
  is lowered to high, and if high is rejected too the field is dropped for that
  model. Limits are kept per model because one provider entry often serves
  models with different ranges.
- /think and config reasoning_effort accept "max". OpenAI reasoning models,
  Gemini and the Codex provider map it like xhigh (Codex previously sent
  xhigh verbatim, which its backend rejects).
